      "figureLabel": "原文 Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2: Overview of GALA. Residuals r_{i} of the host model A with respect to the neutral avatar A(w_{i},\\theta_{0}) (Section 3.2.1) are decomposed by a spatially local, rendering-aware PCA under a memory budget \\mathcal{B} into the block-diagonal basis U (Section 3.2.2). A coefficient network f_{\\phi} is trained to regress the projected coefficients c^{\\star} (Section 3.2.3). At inference, the neutral avatar is computed once per subject, and every frame costs one evaluation of a shallow network f_{\\phi} and a linear blend.",
